Eye Gaze Attention Monitor
Copyright 2026 the Eye Gaze Attention Monitor authors

This project is a desktop-GPU port of "Eye Gaze Attention Monitoring on the
Dragonwing IQ-9075" by Samuel Alexander
(https://github.com/SamuelAlexander/dragonwing-gaze-attention), licensed under the
Apache License 2.0. The pipeline design, pre/post-processing geometry, thresholds and
attention state machine originate there.

Changes from the original:
- Models exported to ONNX and run on NVIDIA GPUs with ONNX Runtime (CUDA), instead
  of TFLite on the Qualcomm Hexagon NPU.
- EyeGaze exported with a dynamic batch and without its unused heatmap output, so
  both eyes run in a single GPU call.
- Threaded webcam capture, non-blocking calibration, H.264 recording, studio and
  pipeline visualisations, live attention timeline, CSV logging, tests.

Models (Qualcomm AI Hub, BSD-3-Clause): EyeGaze, Lightweight-Face-Detection
(face_det_lite), Facial-Landmark-Detection (facemap_3dmm).

Sample media in samples/: see samples/SOURCES.md (Pexels license; Qualcomm AI Hub
demo asset, BSD-3-Clause).
